Changes made in this fork (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):

  2026-10-17  Every file naming the module path was modified: the module path
              github.com/ajroetker/go-highway became github.com/go-simd/highway
              (903 go.mod, .go and .md files). Paths recording where generated
              assembly came from, and benchmark records, were left unchanged.

  2026-10-17  go.mod: the hwy/goat tool is required at a published version
              instead of v0.0.0, which exists nowhere and made
              `go list -m all`, `go mod download all` and gorelease fail for
              every downstream module (ajroetker/go-highway#73; the same change
              upstream is ajroetker/go-highway#74).

The fork exists only so that downstream modules can resolve their module graph
while those upstream changes are pending. It will follow upstream, and end once
upstream releases the fix.
